{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-L3-panel-assistant-01","date":"2026-11-20","lens":"3","surface":"panel","area":"panel/assistant","refs":["FN-L3-panel-screens-1-01"],"severity":"S4","title":"No test proves an owner's AI usage numbers leave out another gym's questions","what":"The AI credits sheet shows who asked the AI this month (owner, staff, members, page visitors) and the gym's question slots. The database tests check these numbers only while no other gym has any questions logged, so nothing would catch a change that started counting another gym's questions. The code keeps gyms apart today.","expected":"A database test logs questions for a second gym and shows the first owner's numbers stay the same.","evidence":["supabase/migrations/0083_ai_members.sql:248-263","supabase/tests/0078_ai_questions.sql:134-141","supabase/tests/0083_ai_members.sql:154-163","apps/dashboard/src/crm/assistant/api.ts:296-298"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"ai-usage-counts-untested-across-gyms","who":"owners","how_often":"only if a future change breaks the gym filter","fix_line":"Add a second gym with logged questions to the AI questions test and check the first owner's numbers do not move","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
